.el .ds Aq '
.TH powerlinux-ocr 1  "PowerLinux 0.1.0" "PowerLinux Manual"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
powerlinux\-ocr \- Select a screen region and copy the recognized text to the clipboard
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpowerlinux ocr\fR [\fB\-\-lang\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Select a screen region and copy the recognized text to the clipboard
.PP
Opens the desktop\*(Aqs interactive screenshot tool through the XDG Screenshot portal, then runs Tesseract on the selected region. Without the portal it falls back to grim+slurp, gnome\-screenshot, spectacle or maim. The text is printed and copied to the clipboard.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fI<LANG>\fR [default: eng]
Tesseract language code(s), e.g. "eng" or "eng+deu"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Recognize English text:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBpowerlinux ocr\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Recognize English and German:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBpowerlinux ocr \-\-lang eng+deu\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Save the text instead of only copying it:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBpowerlinux ocr > notes.txt\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
.PP
Each language needs its Tesseract data package, for example tesseract\-ocr\-deu on Debian and Ubuntu. List the installed ones with tesseract \-\-list\-langs. Leave a small margin around the text when selecting: letters cut by the selection edge are misread.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBpowerlinux\fR(1), \fBtesseract\fR(1)
